course: dictionary
lesson: 1534
title: Certainty: how sure are you?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Certainty is the feeling of being completely sure about something. If you know for certain that it is raining, you have no doubt at all. Nobody can be completely sure of everything, so it is useful to notice how sure a speaker sounds.
explain: A certainty is something that will definitely happen or is definitely true. «The sun will rise tomorrow» is almost a certainty, because we have strong evidence for it. Only use the word when you have good reasons.
explain: Look at the words around certainty to see how strong it is. «It is a theory, not a certainty» tells you the idea might be right, but nobody has proved it. Words like might and may show less sureness, while will and must show more.
fact: Certainty means being completely sure about something.
fact: A certainty is something that will definitely happen or is definitely true.
fact: In maths, a probability of 1 means an event is certain, and a probability of 0 means it is impossible.
fact: Scientists say «with certainty» only when there is strong evidence.
fact: «It's a certainty» and «for a certainty» are phrases that mean definitely.
exercise: «We cannot say with certainty that the bus will be late.» What does «with certainty» mean here? | Only in the evening | Loudly | Very quickly | *Completely sure
exercise: Which word means the feeling of being completely sure? | doubt | guess | *certainty | question
exercise: «The heat death is a theory, not a certainty.» What does this tell us? | It will definitely happen next year | It is a rule of maths that cannot change | *It might be true, but nobody is completely sure | It is a famous song
test: Which modal verb sounds the most sure? | might | could | *will | may
test: «Claiming certainty you don't have is not honest.» What is the honest thing to do? | Pretend to be certain to win | Never say anything at all | *Say how sure you really are | Always claim you are certain
exam: The sun will rise tomorrow, so it is ___. | *a certainty | a guess | a maybe | a wish
